      "id": "b5b16845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The department has prepared a special program for those who wish to engage in a combined study of philosophy and religion. This option emphasizes the comparative and ecumenical study of religion. Students with a general interest in religion might consider this option. Those who wish to pursue a religious vocation or do graduate work in religious studies will find it especially valuable. Advising Notes CR/NC grading is not permitted in courses used to fulfill the philosophy major requirements. Students intending to pursue graduate study in philosophy, law, or religious studies should seek a faculty advisor’s help in planning adequate preparation. In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as: American Government and Institutions ( PLSI 2 ) General Education Requirements (43 units) Additional University Graduation Requirements (9 units) Upper-Division Writing Requirement General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. This includes PHIL 25 (Area 1B). See advisor for details. Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor. A full description of the University’s graduation requirements can be found in the Baccalaureate Degree Requirements .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The department has prepared a special program for those who wish to engage in a combined study of philosophy and religion. This option emphasizes the comparative and ecumenical study of religion. Students with a general interest in religion might consider this option. Those who wish to pursue a religious vocation or do graduate work in religious studies will find it especially valuable.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Advising Notes</strong></p><p class=\"highlight\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">CR/NC grading is not permitted in courses used to fulfill the philosophy major requirements.</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Students intending to pursue graduate study in philosophy, law, or religious studies should seek a faculty advisor’s help in planning adequate preparation.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">In addition to the major program requirements, every student must also complete the University’s baccalaureate degree requirements such as:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">American Government and Institutions (</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3440&amp;returnto=230#tt4883\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PLSI 2</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=249\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirements (43 units)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Additional University Graduation Requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(9 units)</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=245\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Upper-Division Writing</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;Requirement</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Education, Additional University Graduation Requirements and Upper-division Writing courses can be double counted with major requirements. This includes&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=6&amp;poid=3440&amp;returnto=230#tt6093\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">PHIL 25</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;(Area 1B). See advisor for details.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>Sufficient Elective Units to Meet Required Total Units (varies); it is recommended that units in this area be utilized to complete a second major or minor.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">A full description of the University’s graduation requirements can be found in the Baccalaureate&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=234\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Degree Requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">.&nbsp;</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "639b0a24-a602-44d6-9d2f-01982e92b4a8",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Additional University Graduation Requirements The Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education. This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units: Arts/Humanities (A/H) - All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities course to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S) - All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to for graduate at the bachelor’s degree level. Multicultural/International (M/I) - All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate at the bachelor’s degree level.",
      "contentHtml": "<h1>Additional University Graduation Requirements</h1><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The&nbsp;Additional University Graduation Requirements are designed to complement the GE requirements. It is the policy of Fresno State, that all students will cultivate and refine their affective, cognitive, and physical faculties through studying great works of the human imagination; be equipped for lifelong understanding and development of themselves as integrated physiological, social, and psychological beings; and be prepared to understand and live in a multicultural and international world through their undergraduate education.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This will be accomplished through a total of 9 units from the following areas, each requiring 3 units:</span></p><ol><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ah\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Arts/Humanities (A/H)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take an Arts/Humanities&nbsp;course to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#ls\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Lifelong-Understanding and Self-Development (L/S)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All students are required to take a lifelong understanding and self-development course to&nbsp;for graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li><li><a href=\"https://catalog.fresnostate.edu/content.php?catoid=6&amp;navoid=279#mi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Multicultural/International (M/I)</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;All Students are required to take a Multicultural / International course at Fresno State to graduate&nbsp;at the bachelor’s degree level.&nbsp;</span></li></ol>"
    }
